# Demonstrates the optional backpressure feature's 413 response (specs/003-ingestion-backpressure)
# — a batch whose valid entries alone exceed the configured capacity, regardless of any
# other pending work. Only reachable when BACKPRESSURE_ENABLED=true; with the default
# (disabled) configuration, this batch is simply accepted (200).
#
# To reproduce locally:
#   BACKPRESSURE_ENABLED=true BACKPRESSURE_MAX_PENDING_ROWS=1 docker compose up --build -d
# then send this request (2 entries, over the 1-row cap) against a completely idle service.

### Row-count dimension: batch alone exceeds BACKPRESSURE_MAX_PENDING_ROWS
POST http://localhost:8080/logs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "logs": [
    {
      "timestamp": "2026-07-20T14:32:01.123Z",
      "level": "info",
      "service": "backpressure-demo",
      "message": "entry 1",
      "attributes": {}
    },
    {
      "timestamp": "2026-07-20T14:32:01.123Z",
      "level": "info",
      "service": "backpressure-demo",
      "message": "entry 2",
      "attributes": {}
    }
  ]
}

# Expected response (no Retry-After header — retrying the identical batch can never succeed):
#   HTTP/1.1 413 Payload Too Large
#   Content-Type: application/json
#
#   {"error": "batch of 2 entries (~<N> bytes) exceeds the configured ingestion capacity limit and can never be admitted"}

### Byte-size dimension: a single entry alone exceeds BACKPRESSURE_MAX_PENDING_BYTES
# (reproduce with a small BACKPRESSURE_MAX_PENDING_BYTES, e.g. 1kb, and a large enough message)
POST http://localhost:8080/logs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "logs": [
    {
      "timestamp": "2026-07-20T14:32:01.123Z",
      "level": "info",
      "service": "backpressure-demo",
      "message": "a message long enough on its own to exceed a small configured byte cap",
      "attributes": {}
    }
  ]
}
